      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "PET imaging in rats demonstrated that [18F]4FBox crossed the BBB, providing direct in vivo evidence that the benzoxazole-vinyl-dimethylamino scaffold is CNS-permeable.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Rat PET imaging showed 4FBox crossed the BBB, corroborating the scaffold's brain penetration despite not binding fibrils in vivo.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "MicroPET in cynomolgus macaques showed [18F]17b crossed the BBB with high initial brain uptake, extending CNS access evidence to primates for a related fluoroethoxy-substituted heteroaryl tracer.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "In mice, [18F]MA3 showed high brain uptake and was concluded to have good brain uptake, supporting CNS access for related fluoroalkoxy heteroaryl compounds.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All retrieved experimental analogues with high assay-transfer scores show BBB crossing or high brain uptake in rodents and primates; the query shares the key dimethylamino-heteroaryl-vinyl-benzoxazole/fluoroalkoxy features, so meaningful CNS access is predicted.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct quantitative brain-to-plasma or CSF data for the exact query molecule.",
    "No efflux-transporter or P-glycoprotein substrate data for the query.",
    "Most supporting evidence is qualitative PET or biodistribution rather than unbound brain concentration measurements."
  ],
